        "prompt": "$y=3^{x+1}-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Intercepts $(0,1)$ and $(\\log_3 2-1,0)$; asymptote $y=-2$. Increasing.",
          "worked": "Translate $y=3^x$ left by 1 unit and downwards by 2 units.\n\nAt $x=0$, $y=3^1-2=1$.\n\nFor the $x$-intercept:\n$$\\begin{align*}0&=3^{x+1}-2\\\\3^{x+1}&=2\\\\x+1&=\\log_3 2\\\\x&=\\log_3 2-1.\\end{align*}$$\nAs $x\\to-\\infty$, $y\\to-2$ from above. The curve is increasing.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p22-q3k-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"page 22 question 3(k)\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=13mm,y=7mm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (-2.5,0)--(1.5,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-2.8)--(0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[dashed,line width=0.4pt] (-2.5,-2)--(1.4,-2) node[right] {$y=-2$};\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt,domain=-2.5:0.65,samples=80] plot (\\x,{pow(3,\\x+1)-2});\n\\fill (0,1) circle (1.2pt) node[above left] {$(0,1)$};\n\\fill ({ln(2)/ln(3)-1},0) circle (1.2pt) node[above left] {$(\\log_3 2-1,0)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
