        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y$-intercept $(0,-\\tfrac54)$; no $x$-intercept; asymptote $y=-1$. Decreasing.",
          "worked": "Reflect $y=4^x$ in the $x$-axis, then translate right by 1 unit and downwards by 1 unit.\n\nAt $x=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-4^{-1}-1\\\\y&=-\\frac54.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $4^{x-1}>0$, $y<-1$, so there is no $x$-intercept. As $x\\to-\\infty$, $y\\to-1$ from below. The curve is decreasing.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
